    "question": "Which of the following data structures is an example of a non-linear data structure?",
    "options": {
      "A": "Array",
      "B": "Linked List",
      "C": "Stack",
      "D": "Tree"
    },
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "A tree is an example of a non-linear data structure, as it does not have a linear relationship between its elements. In contrast, arrays, linked lists, and stacks are all linear data structures, as they have a linear relationship between their elements.",
