    "question": "What is the time complexity of searching for an element in a binary search tree (BST)?",
    "options": {
      "A": "O(n)",
      "B": "O(log n)",
      "C": "O(n log n)",
      "D": "O(1)"
    },
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "The time complexity of searching for an element in a BST is O(log n), as the BST is a balanced tree and the search operation can be performed in logarithmic time. This is because the BST is constructed in such a way that the height of the tree is logarithmic in the number of elements, and the search operation can take advantage of this property.",
