      "D": "To manage a Last-In-First-Out (LIFO) order of elements"
    },
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "explanation": "A queue is a data structure that follows the First-In-First-Out (FIFO) principle, meaning that the first element that is added to the queue is the first one to be removed. This makes queues useful for managing a sequence of elements in a specific order, such as a line of people waiting for a service.",
